all the codes needed for EELS integrated over the trajectory of the electron using the exponential fit of the EELS as a function of z
 
1) dEELS/dy = A*exp(-2*kappa*(z-h)) where A and kappa are fitting parameters and they depend on the frequency

../bem2D : plot_EELS_fitted_exp.py finds A(omega) and kappa(omega) using the EELS files from datfiles_EELS/along_z

STEP 1) copy fitted_parameters_w500nm_h200nm_N700_Ee200keV_mode1_energy0.7800eV.txt from bem2D/datfiles_EELS/along_z

2) run_potential_and_find_bmin.sh:

                    a) Run e.out to create normalized potential data (list_z_norm_w, listV_normV0)
                    and save the data normalized to U 
                       g++ -o e.out e.cpp
                       files e.cpp and e.h 
                       
                       -first part: finds the value factor = V0/U and uses it to normalize phi/U --> phi/V0
		       -second part: saves data (1 column z/w | 2 column V/V0) 
                     
                    b) Run Python script to obtain bmin(V0,theta)
                       find_bmin_vs_V0_theta.py ---> save data of (V0_solutions, theta_solutions)
 
step 2) upload the V0_solutions/theta_solutions to sonic + potential 


3) integration over z: EELS_integrated_over_z.h (EELS + potential + V0_solutions/theta_solutions) + EELS_integrated_over_z.cpp


4) integration over energy/mode: calculate_total_EELS_vs_theta.py to fit the peaks as a lorentzian and find the width to integrate the EELS over energy

"..fixed_mode" : (Modification for a fixed mode) the energy_list is around a certain mode (see load_energy_from_EELS_files from the .cpp and  "data_modes.txt/README" in bem2d in local computer 


